## core Python (weeks 1 to 4)
     
Cover these topics properly: data types and their methods, list and dictionary comprehensions, functions
and arguments, OOP (classes, inheritance, polymorphism, encapsulation, dunder methods), exception
handling, file handling, modules and packages, virtual environments, decorators, generators, iterators,
and type hints. Type hints matter a lot because FastAPI is built on them.

    
• Learn: CS50P, Harvard's free Python course (cs50.harvard.edu/python), Real Python articles
(realpython.com), the official tutorial (docs.python.org).
• Practise: HackerRank Python track (hackerrank.com), and Python Tutor (pythontutor.com)
whenever you cannot picture what your code is doing.
• GitHub: repo named python_core_practice with one folder per topic. Every topic gets small
programs plus a short notes.md in your own words.
• Done when: you can write a small class based program, for example a library management system in
the terminal, without copying code.

